  "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=\\frac{1}{4}f(x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218586/assets/ed813305ba5087c0b70c6756c2a0b3c7c1957fad1a902e7b1c2540d4f727f3b6.png)",
